# Craft's materials are permanents YOU control and cards in YOUR graveyard (CR 702.167a). Bot2 has an Ornithopter on the
# battlefield and a Black Lotus card in its graveyard; Bot1 has five Mountains and Dire Flail, the Flail its only
# artifact. The Flail can't be its own material ("another artifact"), and the opponent's artifacts are none of Bot1's, so
# the craft ability is not offered (a cost that can't be paid, CR 602.2b). Once Bot1 casts its own Ornithopter, it is
# offered (the positive control), and the choice of materials still leaves out Bot2's Ornithopter and Lotus.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Dire Flail
Ornithopter
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Ornithopter
Black Lotus
Island x20

